module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_counter_acquired_under_one_predicate_and_released_under_another_goes_negative

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// A RESOURCE COUNTER WHOSE INCREMENT IS GUARDED BY ONE PREDICATE AND WHOSE DECREMENT IS GUARDED BY ANOTHER
// DRIFTS, SILENTLY, IN THE DIRECTION THAT MAKES THE NEXT ADMISSION MORE PERMISSIVE. Filed 2026-10-31 by
// proud-bear-756 at the manager's direction (calm-crab-645, msg_b18efa42). The defect was found by
// calm-moth-166 reading the srv1 dev policy and fixed by them in PR #15113 (merged as 6975bc9e610e);
// this row files the CLASS and its executed RED and claims no credit for the fix.

data a_counter_acquired_under_one_predicate_and_released_under_another_goes_negative: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_counter_acquired_under_one_predicate_and_released_under_another_goes_negative" as NonEmptyStr,

  // FOUND SILENTLY WRONG. The figure lives in a shared dictionary read only by a stats endpoint; no request
  // failed because of it, so no case could have seen it through a status code. Silent wrongness is below the
  // ladder, not a rung on it. The ceiling is MechanicallyPreventable: one case refuses the state and it has
  // been executed once by hand.
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the capability of a paired reservation and release to be ONE construct rather than two predicates in two phases -- the shape the modeled front door already has, where the seat's use is opened at admit and ended by front_door_stream_end exactly for the use that opened it -- plus the executed case that refuses any pair which can release a reservation it never made"
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**INVALID STATE.** An access-phase handler reserves a turn only under some predicate, and a log-phase
    handler releases 'the turn' under a DIFFERENT predicate, with nothing shared between them but a name.
    Read in the pre-fix blob at 50043a419018734c846f483c06fb97cc68335fa0 (dag/gunbc/serving/router_dev_policy.dag):
    the reservation is 'begin_turn(u)', which increments 'active:<name>' and refuses past the cap; the release
    is the log phase, 'if ngx.ctx.counted then state:incr(\"active:\" .. ngx.ctx.counted, -1, 0)' (line 482);
    and the flag it keys on is set by 'serve(pick, session)' -- 'ngx.ctx.counted = pick.name' (line 245) --
    not by the reservation. The two guards are not the same test. For a hard engine-local row whose cap is
    the 0 sentinel, the bound-session arm reads 'if hard and bound.cap ~= 0 and not begin_turn(bound)' (line
    315) and so SKIPS begin_turn entirely, then takes 'if hard then return serve(bound, session)' (line 320).
    Every such turn decrements a counter that was never incremented.",

    "**THE CASCADE, IN THE DIRECTION THAT OPENS THE DOOR.** 'active:<name>' walks negative, one per bound
    turn. Every consumer of that figure then reads a permissive value: the pick loop scores
    'local free = c.overflow and 1 or (c.cap - active(c))', so a negative counter turns into FREE CAPACITY
    on a row whose cap the reservation path reads as saturated, and the tie-break prefers the largest free --
    the corrupted row wins selection over rows holding real capacity. And begin_turn's own guard,
    'if not u.overflow and active(u) > u.cap', passes once the counter is negative enough, so a row that was
    being refused for capacity starts admitting. The published figure is wrong in whichever direction the
    drift runs; only the drift that admits is safe to miss.",

    "**WHY IT LOOKED SAFE.** Nothing at the request boundary moves: the session is served, by the engine the
    stickiness rule wanted, with a 200. The counter is a number on a stats page. A case set that asserts
    status codes and routing outcomes cannot see it at all, which is why the class needs a case that asserts
    the COUNTER, not the response.",

    "**THE FIX AS LANDED (calm-moth-166, not this row's claim).** One carrier, set in one place: begin_turn is
    the only reservation and the only setter of the flag the log phase reads -- the merged code states it in
    a comment at that function -- the log phase decrements only when that flag is set, and the forwarded body
    is computed BEFORE any reservation or binding so a refusal leaves no counter and no binding behind.",

    "**THE DISCRIMINATING RED, EXECUTED.** The case 'dev_bound_session_on_a_cap_0_engine_is_refused_and_never_counted'
    in falsifier_cases drives the cap-0 engine_local fixture (f1) with the SAME session twice and asserts four
    things at once: a 429 with 'at its active-turn cap', no upstream line at all, no 'upstream:f1:429' counter,
    and the stats figure 'active:f1' equal to 0 after both turns. At the pre-fix policy the fourth assertion is
    the one that breaks -- the figure reads negative -- which is exactly the manager's requested RED shape:
    that row, that session twice, the counter staying at or above zero.",

    "**WHY THE MODELED ROUTER DOES NOT HAVE THIS FAULT, AND WHERE THE CLASS STILL LIVES.** The front-door model
    pairs the two halves structurally: a seat's use is opened by an admit and ended by
    'front_door_stream_end' against the same grant, so a release cannot outlive an acquire that did not happen
    (gunbc.serving.serving_front_door; capacity admission itself is turn admission,
    gunbc.serving.turn_admission). The class survives anywhere the two halves are written separately -- and
    while routing policy is authored as Lua lines inside 'LuaPhaseBlock' (extdeps.proxy.openresty), they are
    always written separately. So the ceiling is MechanicallyPreventable, not structural, at this substrate.",

    "**CEILING AND TRIGGER.** Blocker ClimbableButUnbuilt: the refusing case exists and has been executed by
    hand on srv1, but the required path runs no claim rows, so today the guarantee holds only while someone
    remembers to run it.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.router_dev_policy", decl_name: "router_dev_access_lines"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.router_dev_policy", decl_name: "router_dev_log_lines"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.instruments.router_proxy_falsifier", decl_name: "falsifier_cases"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.serving_front_door", decl_name: "front_door_stream_end"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.serving.turn_admission", decl_name: "serving_group_admission"),
  ],
}
